WEBVTT FILE

1
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.296
Here, there are flats.

2
00:00:17.296 --> 00:00:20.521
which means that if we have
the money to buy those flats,

3
00:00:20.521 --> 00:00:22.498
then, once we become the owner

4
00:00:22.498 --> 00:00:25.040
we can choose to accommodate
homeless people in it,

5
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.716
We are the owners, we are at home,

6
00:00:26.716 --> 00:00:27.952
we can do what we want.

7
00:00:34.122 --> 00:00:36.370
I was sitting at the terrace of a cafe

8
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.480
when someone begged me for money

9
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.224
Half-heartedly, I gave him a coin

10
00:00:42.224 --> 00:00:45.480
then I wonder: "It’s unbelievable,
this coin I just gave,

11
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.848
will not be really usefull

12
00:00:47.848 --> 00:00:50.820
if we just could manage
to gather more coins

13
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.554
then this guy could have
a roof over his head

14
00:01:04.476 --> 00:01:08.092
Why is this flat
interesting for our organisation ?

15
00:01:08.092 --> 00:01:12.003
It’s because there are two separate rooms

16
00:01:12.003 --> 00:01:15.914
so we could accomodate from
one person to a small family

17
00:01:15.914 --> 00:01:19.827
however it needs to be renovated

18
00:01:19.827 --> 00:01:22.338
but in the end it will make a cosy flat.

19
00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:35.361
When we signed for our first flat,

20
00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:39.773
we were just 30 contributors
and we needed to be 80 to buy it.

21
00:01:39.773 --> 00:01:42.575
regular contributors
are called « godfathers »

22
00:01:42.575 --> 00:01:45.377
they give around 20€ each month

23
00:01:45.377 --> 00:01:48.180
and when we signed the first
purchase agreement, we, Gwen and I,

24
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:54.837
committed ourselves to personally
pay for the missing share.

25
00:01:54.837 --> 00:01:58.473
in fact it took us 3 months
to find the 50 missing godfathers

26
00:01:58.473 --> 00:02:00.483
Once we owned our first flat,

27
00:02:00.483 --> 00:02:03.890
it was easier to convince other people,

28
00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.954
it does exist.

29
00:02:04.954 --> 00:02:08.440
Today, with 500 regular godfathers

30
00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.271
we managed to buy 5 flats

31
00:02:18.881 --> 00:02:22.560
Elisabeth is the first person
we helped with « Toit à Moi »

32
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.761
in the first flat.

33
00:02:24.761 --> 00:02:26.920
- I think of it as a stepping-stone

34
00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.909
Actually, the flat is a stepping-stone

35
00:02:28.909 --> 00:02:32.499
it's like a stepping-stone
to get your own flat

36
00:02:32.499 --> 00:02:36.909
but also the possibility
to build a new social network,

37
00:02:36.909 --> 00:02:40.560
because it was dangerous

38
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.445
when we were outside, it’s just dangerous.

39
00:02:45.445 --> 00:02:50.445
And I think that what could
make people move on,

40
00:02:50.445 --> 00:02:53.594
is to have some new acquaintances

41
00:02:53.594 --> 00:02:56.466
some who don't have those problems

42
00:03:02.988 --> 00:03:07.951
Here at « Toit à Moi »,
what we want is to support people.

43
00:03:10.736 --> 00:03:13.757
I had one meeting every week,
it went very well !

44
00:03:16.778 --> 00:03:19.799
Then we put in place
solutions to go to work

45
00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:23.921
and it helped me to get a
contract to go back to work

46
00:03:23.921 --> 00:03:25.644
and we feel good about ourself

47
00:03:25.644 --> 00:03:27.703
because when you go
to work in the morning,

48
00:03:27.703 --> 00:03:29.532
you just feel like an ordinary person.

49
00:03:35.512 --> 00:03:40.362
People who arrive, are
often exhausted, weakened,

50
00:03:40.362 --> 00:03:44.620
with a lot of things
they gave up because

51
00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:48.071
and because legal procedures
are complicated nowadays

52
00:03:48.071 --> 00:03:51.513
hard to understand and sometimes
you are just fed up to fight

53
00:03:51.513 --> 00:03:55.401
so here I am devoting myself,
to support and reissue their documents

54
00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.920
Update all this with them.

55
00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.460
It's been almost 2 years now that I've
been hosted by the association « Toit à moi »

56
00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.923
Helene helps me with my procedures
because I don’t know how to read,

57
00:04:06.923 --> 00:04:09.423
I don’t know how to read,
I don’t know how to write.

58
00:04:09.423 --> 00:04:12.273
Before, every time I received a mail,
I just threw it away.

59
00:04:12.273 --> 00:04:14.286
Threw Threw Threw …. Junk !

60
00:04:21.849 --> 00:04:23.427
The idea is that a flat

61
00:04:23.427 --> 00:04:25.681
can host someone for about 3 years

62
00:04:25.681 --> 00:04:27.862
but it depends on each one.

63
00:04:27.862 --> 00:04:29.833
Some stay more, some other less

64
00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:31.290
and the person rebounds.

65
00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.711
So after, the same « Toit à Moi »’s
flat can host someone else

66
00:04:33.711 --> 00:04:36.245
then after 3 more years,
someone else and so on…

67
00:04:36.245 --> 00:04:38.359
this could continue for years.

68
00:04:38.359 --> 00:04:41.314
It’s a very human and
very individual approach we take.

69
00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:46.583
We are taking the time to
support everyone depending on their needs.

70
00:04:48.333 --> 00:04:52.414
They don’t depend on funding or politics

71
00:04:52.414 --> 00:04:54.437
which are totally imposed on them

72
00:04:54.437 --> 00:04:57.323
but they are really
taking their time to welcome

73
00:04:57.323 --> 00:05:01.428
and give a quality support to everyone,

74
00:05:01.428 --> 00:05:02.751
so it seduced me

75
00:05:02.751 --> 00:05:07.342
Because it really pushes you to
find a way to achieve

76
00:05:07.342 --> 00:05:09.465
a lasting reintegration

77
00:05:09.465 --> 00:05:11.981
If at the start, there is indignation.

78
00:05:11.981 --> 00:05:14.585
At the root of « Toit à moi » there is an indignation,
but I feel that I acted not just to be indignant.

79
00:05:14.585 --> 00:05:20.555
This indignation, I feel like I acted
not just to be indignated...

80
00:05:20.555 --> 00:05:23.113
it's brave to be indignant but

81
00:05:23.113 --> 00:05:27.162
I feel like I did better than that

82
00:05:27.162 --> 00:05:29.882
and it's really satisfactory.

83
00:05:36.681 --> 00:05:40.824
For more information,
discover the multimedia article

84
00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:46.875
the english version is here :
www.side-ways.net/episode2_en

85
00:05:49.517 --> 00:05:52.830
